<footer>
<p><strong>Mapping notes.</strong> Task 21-31-801 is a DCPC BITE procedure, so the source does not provide the same six fault-isolation headings for it. The three left controller-fault messages under 21-62 all map to Task 802 and share one procedure; they are shown separately because their fault labels differ. Breakers below are those listed by the source task, not an instruction to open them unless the applicable procedure says so.</p>
<p>Source: Boeing 737-600/700/800/900 Fault Isolation Manual, provided by the user, ATA 21. Summarized and paraphrased.</p>
</footer>
</main>
