p("CAB PRESS CON ACFT RATE HI","815","Aircraft climb or descent rate exceeded the pressure-control system's ability to keep pace; the message alone does not indicate a system fault.","Aircraft vertical rate was too high for the pressurization schedule.","SSM/WDM 21-31-22; Airplane Pack Operation Confidence Check, AMM 21-00-05-780-801; Engine Bleed Air System Health Check, AMM 36-11-00-700-801.","Run DCPC BITE Task 801. If the message is absent, treat as intermittent. If BITE history shows Code 30 or flight reports indicate abnormal cabin-altitude behavior, check pack/bleed performance and leakage.","Clear with the DCPC System Test and Clear. If Code 30 or in-flight symptoms persist, verify engine bleed health, pack airflow, and fuselage leakage, then repeat the controller check."),
p("CAB PRESS CON AUTO/MAN ERROR","821","The controller detects a problem with the AUTO/MAN input.","Cabin pressure control module at P5-6 or associated wiring.","SSM/WDM 21-31-11.","Run DCPC BITE Task 801. If the message clears, treat as intermittent; if it remains, continue isolation.","Replace the P5-6 control module and retest. If the message remains, inspect and repair the wiring between both cabin pressure controllers and the module, then repeat BITE."),
p("CAB PRESS CON CAB DIFF PRESS HI","816","Indicates cabin differential pressure above the expected limit.","Outflow valve V48; DCPC No. 1 or No. 2; cabin-altitude/differential-pressure indicator; or flight altitude above the selected FLT ALT value.","SSM/WDM 21-31-22 and 21-31-23; Airplane Pack Operation Confidence Check, AMM 21-00-05-780-801; Engine Bleed Air System Health Check, AMM 36-11-00-700-801.","For specified controller part numbers, inspect copper edge tape and run DCPC BITE. If no message remains, treat as intermittent; follow any additional BITE message.","Use the indicated fault path to assess/replace the outflow valve, controller reporting the fault, and indicator as required, checking BITE after each repair. Confirm the FLT ALT selection; assess pack/bleed performance if symptoms remain."),
