p("CAB PRESS CON LDG GEAR DISAGREE","822","The pressure controllers disagree with the landing-gear/wheels-on-ground signal.","Proximity Switch Electronics Unit (PSEU), M2061, or wiring.","SSM/WDM 21-31-24.","Run DCPC BITE Task 801. If the message clears, treat as intermittent; if it remains, continue with PSEU BITE.","Run PSEU BITE and correct any reported faults. If PSEU BITE is clear, inspect wiring between both pressure controllers and the PSEU, repair as required, and recheck DCPC BITE."),
p("CAB PRESS CON LO INFL/HI LEAKG","823","Indicates low pack-air inflow or excessive cabin leakage; it does not itself indicate a DCPC-system fault.","Low pneumatic pressure; left/right pack flow-control and shutoff valve V18/V19; 35°F low-limit temperature sensor; air-cycle machine; cabin leakage (including cargo-door seals at high differential pressure); or flexible duct.","SSM/WDM 21-51-11; Airplane Pack Operation Confidence Check, AMM 21-00-05-780-801; Engine Bleed Air System Health Check, AMM 36-11-00-700-801.","Run DCPC BITE; if the message is absent, treat as intermittent. With Code 30 or in-flight high-altitude symptoms, check pressure-holding ability, pack airflow, fuselage leakage, and engine bleed performance.","Check for low duct pressure first, then perform pack-flow checks and correct faulty valves/ACM. Investigate cabin leaks and flexible ducts. If high cabin altitude occurred in flight, inspect cargo-door seals before opening the doors because a deformed seal may recover after opening."),
